#: class-table-sort.php:121
msgid "The heading text for the table column that this facet is placed above. Can contain HTML. By default it will display to the left of the sort icons and will trigger a sort reset when clicked. If left empty, only the sort icons will be displayed. The heading text is also used in User Selections and title attributes (tooltips) if the Sort label is left empty."
msgstr ""

#: class-table-sort.php:130
msgid "Sort column by"
msgstr ""

#: class-table-sort.php:131
msgid "Choose the field to sort this table column by. Both sort directions (ASC and DESC) are created automatically, so you don't need to add a descending sort yourself. Optionally, click + to add a secondary (fallback) sort for items with equal values. Its order (ASC or DESC) is used in both sort directions. The sort label is used in the User Selections facet and in the sort options' title attributes (tooltips), e.g. 'Sort by {sort label} (asc)'. If it is empty, the 'Table column heading' text is used instead. Don't leave both settings empty. To display only the column heading, for a column that should not be sortable, remove the sort option with the − icon and add a heading text."
msgstr ""

